# Client (Vite) environment. Copy this file to .env.local at the repo root — Vite loads
# .env.local automatically and it's gitignored, same as api/.env.
#
# Not required for local development: the Vite dev server proxies /api/* to the backend
# on http://127.0.0.1:8000 (see vite.config.ts), so the client calls same-origin
# /api/v1/... with no base URL needed. Only set this for a split-domain deployment where
# the client and API are on different origins (e.g. Render — see docs/deployment.md).
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
